  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q9-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "How many ways can five different letters be distributed to five letterboxes so that the first or second letterbox is empty?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$1805$ ways.\n\nAdd the counts with either letterbox empty, then subtract the count with both empty.",
      "worked": "Let $A$ be the distributions with the first letterbox empty and $B$ those with the second letterbox empty. Each letter independently goes into one of the available letterboxes.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}|A| &= 4^5 = 1024\\\\|B| &= 4^5 = 1024\\\\|A\\cap B| &= 3^5 = 243\\\\|A\\cup B| &= |A|+|B|-|A\\cap B|\\\\|A\\cup B| &= 1024+1024-243\\\\|A\\cup B| &= 1805\\end{align*}$$\n\nThere are $1805$ ways.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 38
  },
